{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Synonym groups for symptom names. Diary entries and syndrome profiles are mapped to the canonical name before matching, so e.g. 'Myalgie' in a profile and 'Muskelschmerzen' in a diary count as the same symptom.",
    "rules": [
      "Only true synonyms or a narrower term mapped to the broader profile term (e.g. 'Insomnie' -> 'Schlafstörungen'). Related but different symptoms stay separate (e.g. 'Herzrasen' vs. 'Palpitationen', 'Herzstolpern').",
      "Ambiguous terms are left out (e.g. 'Taubheit' = numbness or deafness, 'Brennen').",
      "Combined diary entries (e.g. 'Brainfog/Konzentrationsstörungen' from symptom_map.json) are listed under 'combined' and match every profile symptom in 'maps_to'.",
      "A diary entry that can mean a milder or a more severe symptom maps only to the milder one: 'Ohnmacht/Benommenheit' -> 'Schwindel', not 'Synkope', because the entry does not say whether a real syncope happened.",
      "Each variant belongs to exactly one group. Matching is case-insensitive and ignores surrounding whitespace.",
      "The canonical name is the spelling used most often in the syndrome profiles.",
      "Raw diary names are first mapped via config/symptom_map.json (or the user copy in ~/.config/kyoro/), then via these groups."
    ],
    "used_by": "scripts/modules/symptom_synonyms.py"
  },
